From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: odonnellmatt <odonnellmatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:01:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/pad: a self-test for the layout editor
 (DM_PAD_LAYOUT_TEST)

The layout editor's gestures are UIKit code, which no test on Linux or in
CI runs. DM_PAD_LAYOUT_TEST=1 (in Documents/env.txt, or in a game's env.txt
in the shell) runs a scripted pass through the editor on the device. Three
seconds after the touch gamepad's first layout it opens the editor, taps
Both sides together on the panel, drags the left shoulders down by 30 % of
their free range in ten steps (the right ones follow), taps Each side on
its own and drags the left ones half of the way back up (the right ones
stay), taps Both sides together again (nothing moves), pinches A B X Y
toward 120 % (the stick goes along as far as it has room), taps the D-pad
(in 2D the middle group: the choice must be dimmed there) and sets its
slider to 80 %, sets all controls to 105 % and taps Done, each step through
the method a finger, the pinch or the panel calls (the choice through the
action a tap on it sends). It logs every control's frame before and after,
reads the value back from where Done saved it, and checks that the geometry
of that value alone, and the gamepad's own, give the same frames and send
every touch point to the control it lies in. Then it puts back what was
stored before; with nothing stored before, it leaves nothing stored
(through the hosting app's _forget hook; without that hook it stores the
built-in layout and the log says so). On a screen where the shoulders have
no room to come down it says so and skips that check. Its lines start with
"pad layout test:", a failure is a [RED] line, and the last line says PASS
or FAIL. dm_pad_layout_self_test() runs it at once, for the Duo harness.

Checked here (Linux, no Apple SDK): pad_groups_check.m replays the script
through DmPadEditing.h's rules on 810 combinations (every screen, 2D and
3D, every size and stick place, three arrangements); 48 have no room to
lower the shoulders and are skipped, as the self-test skips them; none
fails; also under gcc ASan and UBSan. DmGamepad.m passes the stub syntax
check; test_pad_geometry.py, env_switches.py --check, test_docs.py. A new
Duo harness test runs the self-test on three screens in 2D and 3D and
checks that the stored value comes back.

Run on a Mac, on the author's own tree (this series' feature code on
another base) with the whole series applied: testLayoutEditorSelfTestPasses
passed on Simulators of an iPhone SE (3rd generation), an iPhone 17, an
iPhone 17 Pro Max and an 11-inch iPad. Not run: this exact tree on a Mac,
DM_PAD_LAYOUT_TEST on a real device.

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on 0020 and 0040: the seedds/nxnative pull request follows once they are upstream]
Reason: a scripted self-test of the layout editor on the device (DM_PAD_LAYOUT_TEST), since no CI runs its UIKit code
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#ISSUE (the feature issue, to be opened before the pull request)

